            <note corresp="#d440-f2" n="2" xml:id="d440-f2-content">
                <p>For text dated December 19, see SC, <hi rendition="#italic">3rd yr., Suppl.</hi>
                    (Dec.), p. 224.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d440-f3" n="3" xml:id="d440-f3-content">
                <p>Telegram 1117, <hi rendition="#italic">infra.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d440-f4" n="4" xml:id="d440-f4-content">
                <p>As 1671, 281, 154, 4706, 648, and 672 (Usgoc 252), respectively. In telegram
                    5310, December 20, 6 p. m., from London, the Embassy reported the British
                    Foreign Secretary “expressed desire to go along with US in every way possible
                    but who was opposed to sanctions.” (856d.00/12–2048)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
